00:39:06,481 --> 00:39:08,860
I mean, no one really else does that,

529
00:39:08,861 --> 00:39:11,280
so they don't know what to expect.

530
00:39:13,500 --> 00:39:17,100
Through shooting, Randy has learned lessons for life.

531
00:39:19,240 --> 00:39:21,100
I've learned a lot of discipline,

532
00:39:21,101 --> 00:39:23,380
and I've learned to focus.

533
00:39:23,381 --> 00:39:26,140
Like when I have a job, I'll be more stick to it

534
00:39:26,141 --> 00:39:26,980
kind of thing.

535
00:39:33,940 --> 00:39:36,040
The shotgun has come full circle

536
00:39:36,041 --> 00:39:38,300
since its days as a royal fowler

537
00:39:38,301 --> 00:39:41,180
that peaked in the late 1800s.

538
00:39:41,181 --> 00:39:45,320
Legendary British gun makers such as Purdy, Boss,

539
00:39:45,321 --> 00:39:48,280
and Holland and Holland handcrafted guns

540
00:39:48,281 --> 00:39:52,160
that were as much works of art as tools for sport.

541
00:39:53,100 --> 00:39:55,960
They had figured out something that was very esoteric,

542
00:39:55,961 --> 00:39:58,700
which was that they had brought the gun down

543
00:39:58,701 --> 00:40:02,660
to where it became part of your body.

544
00:40:02,661 --> 00:40:05,000
And you really didn't think all

545
00:40:05,001 --> 00:40:08,500
looking down the barrels, you simply looked at the target

546
00:40:08,501 --> 00:40:11,780
and the gun swung perfectly and moved perfectly

547
00:40:11,781 --> 00:40:14,480
and you just fired it at your will,

548
00:40:14,481 --> 00:40:17,820
so it was really your mind willing that bird

549
00:40:17,821 --> 00:40:19,340
to fall out of the sky.

550
00:40:19,341 --> 00:40:22,580
And when you're shooting really well with one of those guns,

551
00:40:22,581 --> 00:40:26,180
it's almost like that, you just simply say, that one.

552
00:40:26,181 --> 00:40:27,420
And it's almost like you point,

553
00:40:27,421 --> 00:40:29,760
it falls out of the sky with your finger.

554
00:40:29,761 --> 00:40:31,860
You're not even aware of shooting the gun.

555
00:40:31,861 --> 00:40:39,360
Today, the most magnificent shotguns are again made in Europe and are valued for both their

556
00:40:39,361 --> 00:40:42,620
form and function.

557
00:40:42,621 --> 00:40:48,740
Italy is now in the forefront of quality and artistry because they have the finest engravers,

558
00:40:48,741 --> 00:40:55,840
Torquely, Fricasse, and they have the great gun makers, Fabri, Parazzi and Beretta.

559
00:40:55,841 --> 00:40:56,840
This is a Rizzini.

560
00:40:56,841 --> 00:41:02,980
A gun like this is an extraordinary work of art as well as an extremely functional gun.

561
00:41:02,981 --> 00:41:08,500
But our 18th century or 17th century wildfowler would be very much at home using this

562
00:41:08,501 --> 00:41:11,880
because it hasn't really changed that much in 400 years.

563
00:41:13,240 --> 00:41:17,000
Mauro Parazzi is a second generation gunmaker from Italy.

564
00:41:20,800 --> 00:41:26,220
The tradition that is our mark, our emblem, was founded by my father about 40 years ago.

565
00:41:26,221 --> 00:41:30,580
The result is a combination of tradition with enough new and recent.

566
00:41:31,220 --> 00:41:35,860
And obviously we are the ones who have searched to achieve that which has been learned in the past,

567
00:41:35,980 --> 00:41:40,080
to bring into the present, and therefore to carry it into the future.

568
00:41:44,640 --> 00:41:48,800
Parazzi's customers can choose from a wide variety of types and styles.

569
00:41:49,520 --> 00:41:54,140
The guns are then custom-fit to the buyer's size and adjusted to his shooting habits.

570
00:41:56,220 --> 00:41:59,360
The shotgun I'm showing now, I believe,

571
00:41:59,361 --> 00:42:02,020
remains my favorite shotgun.

572
00:42:02,021 --> 00:42:04,000
My favorite for several reasons.

573
00:42:04,001 --> 00:42:06,300
Overall is the fact of the engravings,

574
00:42:06,301 --> 00:42:11,260
